]sase-b1[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-b1/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Carry the swarm chain on expansion records[/bold #D7AFFF]                    [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]swarm-provenance[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]swarm-provenance: add an ordered outer-to-inner swarm-name chain to the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]expanded-segment record in sase/agent/xprompt_swarm.py, populated in all[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]four expansion branches and inherited unchanged by pass-through [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]segments, without altering template-group behavior.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Thread provenance to the spawn point[/bold #D7AFFF]                          [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]launch-env-plumbing[dim] · [dim][/dim]after swarm-provenance[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]launch-env-plumbing: thread the per-segment swarm chain through the CLI [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and ACE launch paths alongside segment_template_groups, inject it into [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]each spawned slot's environment like SASE_MULTI_AGENT_PROMPT_FILE, cover[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the single-segment fall-throughs, and scrub it from nested launches.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Teach the Rust scanner the swarm kind[/bold #D7AFFF]                         [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]core-swarm-kind[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]core-swarm-kind: in the sibling sase-core repo, normalize a \"swarm\" kind[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]in the agent-scan xprompts.json loader so it survives into the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]statistics 